# Project documentation (agent orientation)

At the **start** of tasks in this workspace, read the relevant map:

- **NAS bridge / container (Node):** `src/PROJECT.md`
- **Windows display client (Python):** `alexa broadcast client/src/PROJECT.md`

These files summarize architecture, data flow, config, UDP protocol v2, tests, and deployment. Use them instead of re-scanning the whole repo when possible.

## Keep docs fresh

When you change **architecture, modules, config keys, Docker/auth workflows, UDP protocol, overlay UI, packaging, or tests**:

1. Update the matching `PROJECT.md` in the **same change** (both if the change spans bridge + client).
2. Bump the **Last updated** date at the top.
3. Add a one-line bullet under **Recent changes** (newest first).

Do not duplicate `README.md` or `DOCKER.md` — those are user guides; `PROJECT.md` is the agent quick-reference.

If unsure whether a change warrants an update, update anyway when behavior or file roles changed.

## Testing (required)

| Suite | Command | Location |
|-------|---------|----------|
| **Full (bridge + client)** | `run_all_tests.bat` | Repo root |
| Bridge only | `npm test` | Repo root — Node built-in test runner (`test/*.test.js`) |
| Client only | `alexa broadcast client\test\run_tests.bat` | Python `unittest` — `test_*.py` |

